  "content": "<b>Meaning/Usage</b>: Used to tell someone that they will not get what they want.\n<b>Explanation</b>: Although the sentences below are used in full sentences, this phrase is commonly used by itself.\n\"Sure you will be a millionaire one day, <b>in your dreams</b>.\"\n\"You will be as good as me <b>in your dreams</b>.\"\n\"You think you will beat me? <b>In your dreams</b>.\"\n<b>A.</b> \"I've been practicing shooting basketball with my dad.\"\n<b>B.</b> \"Are you getting any better?\"\n<b>A.</b> \"I can beat you now.\"\n<b>B.</b> \"<b>In your dreams</b>, buddy!\"\nOther Common Sentences\n\"You wish.\"",
